{"id":"mahabharata-5-033","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":33,"title":"त्रयस्त्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 33 · Vidura's counsel: the wise and the foolish","summary":{"en":"Sleepless with anxiety, Dhritarashtra summons Vidura at night and asks for counsel. Vidura describes the marks of the wise and the foolish, the virtues of a good king and the faults that destroy men, and urges him to give the Pandavas their due share and live happily with his sons.","kn":"ಆತಂಕದಿಂದ ನಿದ್ರೆಯಿಲ್ಲದ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನು ರಾತ್ರಿ ವಿದುರನನ್ನು ಕರೆಸಿ ಸಲಹೆ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಜ್ಞಾನಿ ಮೂರ್ಖರ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳನ್ನೂ ಸದ್ರಾಜನ ಗುಣಗಳನ್ನೂ ಮನುಷ್ಯರನ್ನು ನಾಶಮಾಡುವ ದೋಷಗಳನ್ನೂ ವಿದುರನು ವರ್ಣಿಸಿ, ಪಾಂಡವರಿಗೆ ಉಚಿತ ಪಾಲು ನೀಡಿ ಮಕ್ಕಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಸುಖವಾಗಿರು ಎಂದು ಒತ್ತಾಯಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"चिन्ता से अनिद्र धृतराष्ट्र रात में विदुर को बुलाकर सलाह माँगते हैं। विदुर ज्ञानी और मूर्ख के लक्षणों, अच्छे राजा के गुणों और मनुष्यों का नाश करने वाले दोषों का वर्णन करते हैं, और आग्रह करते हैं कि वे पाण्डवों को उनका उचित भाग देकर पुत्रों के साथ सुख से रहें।","te":"ఆందోళనతో నిద్రలేని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు రాత్రి విదురుని పిలిపించి సలహా అడుగుతాడు. జ్ఞానుల, మూర్ఖుల లక్షణాలను, మంచి రాజు గుణాలను, మనుషులను నాశనం చేసే దోషాలను విదురుడు వర్ణించి, పాండవులకు న్యాయమైన వాటా ఇచ్చి కుమారులతో సుఖంగా ఉండమని కోరతాడు.","ta":"கவலையால் உறக்கமற்ற த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் இரவில் விதுரரை அழைத்து அறிவுரை கேட்கிறான். ஞானி, மூடரின் அடையாளங்களையும், நல்ல மன்னனின் பண்புகளையும், மனிதரை அழிக்கும் குறைகளையும் விதுரர் விவரித்து, பாண்டவர்களுக்கு உரிய பங்கைக் கொடுத்து மைந்தர்களுடன் மகிழ்வாக வாழுமாறு வற்புறுத்துகிறார்.","ml":"ഉത്കണ്ഠകൊണ്ട് ഉറങ്ങാനാകാതെ ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ രാത്രിയിൽ വിദുരരെ വിളിച്ച് ഉപദേശം തേടുന്നു. ജ്ഞാനികളുടെയും മൂഢന്മാരുടെയും ലക്ഷണങ്ങളും, നല്ല രാജാവിന്റെ ഗുണങ്ങളും മനുഷ്യരെ നശിപ്പിക്കുന്ന ദോഷങ്ങളും വിദുരർ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. പാണ്ഡവർക്ക് അവരുടെ അർഹമായ ഓഹരി നൽകി, മക്കളോടൊപ്പം സന്തോഷത്തോടെ കഴിയാൻ അദ്ദേഹം ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.33; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"प्रजागरपर्व","titleEn":"Prajagara Parva (The sleepless night)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"द्वाःस्थं प्राह महाप्राज्ञो धृतराष्ट्रो महीपतिः ।\nविदुरं द्रष्टुमिच्छामि तमिहानय माचिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The very wise king Dhritarashtra said to his doorkeeper, \"I wish to see Vidura; bring him here without delay.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रहितो धृतराष्ट्रेण दूतः क्षत्तारमब्रवीत् ।\nईश्वरस्त्वां महाराजो महाप्राज्ञ दिदृक्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sent by Dhritarashtra, the messenger said to Kshatta, \"The great king, the lord, wishes to see you, O man of great wisdom.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु विदुरः प्राप्य राजनिवेशनम् ।\nअब्रवीद्धृतराष्ट्राय द्वाःस्थ मां प्रतिवेदय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus told, Vidura reached the king's residence and said to the doorkeeper, \"Announce me to Dhritarashtra.\""}},{"text":"द्वाःस्थ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The doorkeeper said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"विदुरोऽयमनुप्राप्तो राजेन्द्र तव शासनात् ।\nद्रष्टुमिच्छति ते पादौ किं करोतु प्रशाधि माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is Vidura, king of kings, arrived at your command. He wishes to see your feet; tell me what he is to do."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"प्रवेशय महाप्राज्ञं विदुरं दीर्घदर्शिनम् ।\nअहं हि विदुरस्यास्य नाकाल्यो जातु दर्शने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bring in the very wise, far-seeing Vidura. I am never unavailable to see Vidura."}},{"text":"द्वाःस्थ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The doorkeeper said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रविशान्तःपुरं क्षत्तर्महाराजस्य धीमतः ।\nन हि ते दर्शनेऽकाल्यो जातु राजा ब्रवीति माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enter the inner apartments, Kshatta, of the wise great king. The king has told me that he is never unavailable for your visit."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः प्रविश्य विदुरो धृतराष्ट्रनिवेशनम् ।\nअब्रवीत्प्राञ्जलिर्वाक्यं चिन्तयानं नराधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vidura entered Dhritarashtra's residence and, with folded hands, spoke to the king as he sat brooding."}},{"n":8,"text":"विदुरोऽहं महाप्राज्ञ संप्राप्तस्तव शासनात् ।\nयदि किंचन कर्तव्यमयमस्मि प्रशाधि माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am Vidura, O man of great wisdom, come at your command. If there is anything to be done, here I am; instruct me."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"संजयो विदुर प्राप्तो गर्हयित्वा च मां गतः ।\nअजातशत्रोः श्वो वाक्यं सभामध्ये स वक्ष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya has come back, Vidura, after rebuking me; tomorrow he will speak the words of Ajatashatru in the midst of the assembly."}},{"n":10,"text":"तस्याद्य कुरुवीरस्य न विज्ञातं वचो मया ।\nतन्मे दहति गात्राणि तदकार्षीत्प्रजागरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today I have not learned what that hero of the Kurus said, and that burns my limbs and has kept me awake."}},{"n":11,"text":"जाग्रतो दह्यमानस्य श्रेयो यदिह पश्यसि ।\nतद्ब्रूहि त्वं हि नस्तात धर्मार्थकुशलो ह्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me what you think is best here for one who lies awake and burns; dear friend, you are skilled in dharma and in worldly gain."}},{"n":12,"text":"यतः प्राप्तः संजयः पाण्डवेभ्यो\nन मे यथावन्मनसः प्रशान्तिः ।\nसर्वेन्द्रियाण्यप्रकृतिं गतानि\nकिं वक्ष्यतीत्येव हि मेऽद्य चिन्ता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since Sanjaya came back from the Pandavas my mind has had no real peace; all my senses are out of their natural state, and my worry today is only what he will say."}},{"text":"विदुर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vidura said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"अभियुक्तं बलवता दुर्बलं हीनसाधनम् ।\nहृतस्वं कामिनं चोरमाविशन्ति प्रजागराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sleeplessness comes upon one who is attacked by a stronger man, the weak man without resources, the one robbed of his goods, the lustful man, and the thief."}},{"n":14,"text":"कच्चिदेतैर्महादोषैर्न स्पृष्टोऽसि नराधिप ।\nकच्चिन्न परवित्तेषु गृध्यन्विपरितप्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I hope, king, that you are not touched by these great faults, and that you are not tormented by longing for the wealth of others."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"श्रोतुमिच्छामि ते धर्म्यं परं नैःश्रेयसं वचः ।\nअस्मिन्राजर्षिवंशे हि त्वमेकः प्राज्ञसंमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to hear your words, which are righteous and lead to the highest good, for in this family of royal sages you alone are honored as wise."}},{"text":"विदुर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vidura said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"निषेवते प्रशस्तानि निन्दितानि न सेवते ।\nअनास्तिकः श्रद्दधान एतत्पण्डितलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who follows what is praised and avoids what is blamed, who is not a nonbeliever and has faith: this is the mark of a wise man."}},{"n":17,"text":"क्रोधो हर्षश्च दर्पश्च ह्रीस्तम्भो मान्यमानिता ।\nयमर्थान्नापकर्षन्ति स वै पण्डित उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whom anger, joy, pride, shame, stubbornness and conceit do not pull away from his aims is called wise."}},{"n":18,"text":"यस्य कृत्यं न जानन्ति मन्त्रं वा मन्त्रितं परे ।\nकृतमेवास्य जानन्ति स वै पण्डित उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whose plans and intentions others do not know beforehand, but only after they are carried out, is called wise."}},{"n":19,"text":"यस्य कृत्यं न विघ्नन्ति शीतमुष्णं भयं रतिः ।\nसमृद्धिरसमृद्धिर्वा स वै पण्डित उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whose undertaking is not blocked by cold or heat, fear or pleasure, wealth or lack of it, is called wise."}},{"n":20,"text":"यस्य संसारिणी प्रज्ञा धर्मार्थावनुवर्तते ।\nकामादर्थं वृणीते यः स वै पण्डित उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whose practical wisdom follows dharma and worldly aims, and who chooses what is useful over what is desired, is called wise."}},{"n":21,"text":"यथाशक्ति चिकीर्षन्ति यथाशक्ति च कुर्वते ।\nन किंचिदवमन्यन्ते पण्डिता भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise men, bull of the Bharatas, want to do what they can and do it as far as they can; they despise nothing."}},{"n":22,"text":"क्षिप्रं विजानाति चिरं शृणोति\nविज्ञाय चार्थं भजते न कामात् ।\nनासंपृष्टो व्युपयुङ्क्ते परार्थे\nतत्प्रज्ञानं प्रथमं पण्डितस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"He understands quickly and listens long; having understood, he acts from purpose, not desire; and he does not meddle in another's affairs unasked. This is the first sign of a wise man's wisdom."}},{"n":23,"text":"नाप्राप्यमभिवाञ्छन्ति नष्टं नेच्छन्ति शोचितुम् ।\nआपत्सु च न मुह्यन्ति नराः पण्डितबुद्धयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men of wise minds do not long for what cannot be obtained, do not wish to grieve over what is lost, and do not lose their heads in misfortune."}},{"n":24,"text":"निश्चित्य यः प्रक्रमते नान्तर्वसति कर्मणः ।\nअवन्ध्यकालो वश्यात्मा स वै पण्डित उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who sets to work after deciding, who does not stop in the middle of a task, who wastes no time and has himself in hand, is called wise."}},{"n":25,"text":"आर्यकर्मणि रज्यन्ते भूतिकर्माणि कुर्वते ।\nहितं च नाभ्यसूयन्ति पण्डिता भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise men, bull of the Bharatas, delight in noble works, undertake tasks that bring prosperity, and do not resent what is good for them."}},{"n":26,"text":"न हृष्यत्यात्मसंमाने नावमानेन तप्यते ।\nगाङ्गो ह्रद इवाक्षोभ्यो यः स पण्डित उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who does not rejoice at being honored and is not pained by contempt, calm like the lake of the Ganga, is called wise."}},{"n":27,"text":"तत्त्वज्ञः सर्वभूतानां योगज्ञः सर्वकर्मणाम् ।\nउपायज्ञो मनुष्याणां नरः पण्डित उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who knows the truth of all beings, who knows the way of all actions, and knows the means among men is called wise."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्रवृत्तवाक्चित्रकथ ऊहवान्प्रतिभानवान् ।\nआशु ग्रन्थस्य वक्ता च स वै पण्डित उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who is ready of speech, tells varied tales, has reasoning and quick insight, and can quickly explain a text is called wise."}},{"n":29,"text":"श्रुतं प्रज्ञानुगं यस्य प्रज्ञा चैव श्रुतानुगा ।\nअसंभिन्नार्यमर्यादः पण्डिताख्यां लभेत सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whose learning follows his intelligence and whose intelligence follows his learning, and who does not break the noble limits, deserves the name of wise."}},{"n":30,"text":"अश्रुतश्च समुन्नद्धो दरिद्रश्च महामनाः ।\nअर्थांश्चाकर्मणा प्रेप्सुर्मूढ इत्युच्यते बुधैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is unlearned, puffed up and poor, yet proud, and who tries to get wealth without work, is called a fool by the wise."}},{"n":31,"text":"स्वमर्थं यः परित्यज्य परार्थमनुतिष्ठति ।\nमिथ्या चरति मित्रार्थे यश्च मूढः स उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who abandons his own interest to pursue another's, and who acts falsely toward a friend, is called a fool."}},{"n":32,"text":"अकामान्कामयति यः कामयानान्परिद्विषन् ।\nबलवन्तं च यो द्वेष्टि तमाहुर्मूढचेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who desires those who do not desire him, and hates those who desire him, and who hates the strong, they call dull-minded."}},{"n":33,"text":"अमित्रं कुरुते मित्रं मित्रं द्वेष्टि हिनस्ति च ।\nकर्म चारभते दुष्टं तमाहुर्मूढचेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who makes an enemy a friend, hates and harms a friend, and begins bad deeds, they call dull-minded."}},{"n":34,"text":"संसारयति कृत्यानि सर्वत्र विचिकित्सते ।\nचिरं करोति क्षिप्रार्थे स मूढो भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who drags out tasks, doubts everywhere, and is slow in what needs speed is a fool, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":35,"text":"अनाहूतः प्रविशति अपृष्टो बहु भाषते ।\nविश्वसत्यप्रमत्तेषु मूढचेता नराधमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who enters uninvited, talks much unasked, and trusts those who are not careful is a dull-minded, lowest of men."}},{"n":36,"text":"परं क्षिपति दोषेण वर्तमानः स्वयं तथा ।\nयश्च क्रुध्यत्यनीशः सन्स च मूढतमो नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who throws blame on another while he himself acts the same, and who gets angry though powerless, is the greatest of fools."}},{"n":37,"text":"आत्मनो बलमज्ञाय धर्मार्थपरिवर्जितम् ।\nअलभ्यमिच्छन्नैष्कर्म्यान्मूढबुद्धिरिहोच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who does not know his own strength, is without dharma and wealth, and wants what cannot be had without effort, is here called foolish in mind."}},{"n":38,"text":"अशिष्यं शास्ति यो राजन्यश्च शून्यमुपासते ।\nकदर्यं भजते यश्च तमाहुर्मूढचेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who instructs one who will not learn, who attends on an empty man, and who serves a miser, they call dull-minded, king."}},{"n":39,"text":"अर्थं महान्तमासाद्य विद्यामैश्वर्यमेव वा ।\nविचरत्यसमुन्नद्धो यः स पण्डित उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who, having gained great wealth, learning or lordship, goes about without arrogance is called wise."}},{"n":40,"text":"एकः संपन्नमश्नाति वस्ते वासश्च शोभनम् ।\nयोऽसंविभज्य भृत्येभ्यः को नृशंसतरस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who eats good food alone and wears fine clothes alone, without sharing with his dependents, who is more cruel than he?"}},{"n":41,"text":"एकः पापानि कुरुते फलं भुङ्क्ते महाजनः ।\nभोक्तारो विप्रमुच्यन्ते कर्ता दोषेण लिप्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One man does wrong, and many enjoy the fruit; the enjoyers are freed, but the doer is stained with the fault."}},{"n":42,"text":"एकं हन्यान्न वा हन्यादिषुर्मुक्तो धनुष्मता ।\nबुद्धिर्बुद्धिमतोत्सृष्टा हन्याद्राष्ट्रं सराजकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"An arrow shot by an archer may or may not kill one man; but a plan shot by a clever mind can destroy a kingdom with its king."}},{"n":43,"text":"एकया द्वे विनिश्चित्य त्रींश्चतुर्भिर्वशे कुरु ।\nपञ्च जित्वा विदित्वा षट्सप्त हित्वा सुखी भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"By one decide two, bring three under control by four, having conquered five and known six, leave seven and be happy."}},{"n":44,"text":"एकं विषरसो हन्ति शस्त्रेणैकश्च वध्यते ।\nसराष्ट्रं सप्रजं हन्ति राजानं मन्त्रविस्रवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Poison kills only one, a weapon kills one person; but a leaked counsel kills a king along with his kingdom and people."}},{"n":45,"text":"एकः स्वादु न भुञ्जीत एकश्चार्थान्न चिन्तयेत् ।\nएको न गच्छेदध्वानं नैकः सुप्तेषु जागृयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man should not eat sweets alone, should not think over affairs alone, should not travel alone, and should not stay awake alone among sleepers."}},{"n":46,"text":"एकमेवाद्वितीयं तद्यद्राजन्नावबुध्यसे ।\nसत्यं स्वर्गस्य सोपानं पारावारस्य नौरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is one thing, without a second, which you do not grasp, king: truth, the stairway to heaven, like a boat for the sea."}},{"n":47,"text":"एकः क्षमावतां दोषो द्वितीयो नोपलभ्यते ।\nयदेनं क्षमया युक्तमशक्तं मन्यते जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the one fault of the forgiving, and no second is found: that people think a forgiving man is weak."}},{"n":48,"text":"एको धर्मः परं श्रेयः क्षमैका शान्तिरुत्तमा ।\nविद्यैका परमा दृष्टिरहिंसैका सुखावहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharma alone is the highest good, forbearance alone is the best peace, knowledge alone is the supreme sight, and non-violence alone brings happiness."}},{"n":49,"text":"द्वाविमौ ग्रसते भूमिः सर्पो बिलशयानिव ।\nराजानं चाविरोद्धारं ब्राह्मणं चाप्रवासिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth swallows these two, as a snake does the creatures in a hole: a king who does not resist and a brahmin who does not travel."}},{"n":50,"text":"द्वे कर्मणी नरः कुर्वन्नस्मिँल्लोके विरोचते ।\nअब्रुवन्परुषं किंचिदसतो नार्थयंस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By doing two things a man shines in this world: speaking nothing harsh and not favoring the wicked."}},{"n":51,"text":"द्वाविमौ पुरुषव्याघ्र परप्रत्ययकारिणौ ।\nस्त्रियः कामितकामिन्यो लोकः पूजितपूजकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two, tiger among men, act on the belief of others: women who love one who loves them, and the world that honors one who is honored."}},{"n":52,"text":"द्वाविमौ कण्टकौ तीक्ष्णौ शरीरपरिशोषणौ ।\nयश्चाधनः कामयते यश्च कुप्यत्यनीश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two are sharp thorns that dry up the body: the poor man who has desires, and the powerless man who gets angry."}},{"n":53,"text":"द्वाविमौ पुरुषौ राजन्स्वर्गस्योपरि तिष्ठतः ।\nप्रभुश्च क्षमया युक्तो दरिद्रश्च प्रदानवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two men, king, stand above heaven: a mighty man who is forgiving and a poor man who gives."}},{"n":54,"text":"न्यायागतस्य द्रव्यस्य बोद्धव्यौ द्वावतिक्रमौ ।\nअपात्रे प्रतिपत्तिश्च पात्रे चाप्रतिपादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Two transgressions are to be understood in wealth justly gained: giving to an unworthy person and not giving to a worthy one."}},{"n":55,"text":"त्रयो न्याया मनुष्याणां श्रूयन्ते भरतर्षभ ।\nकनीयान्मध्यमः श्रेष्ठ इति वेदविदो विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three standards for men are heard of, bull of the Bharatas: lowest, middle, best, so the knowers of the Veda say."}},{"n":56,"text":"त्रिविधाः पुरुषा राजन्नुत्तमाधममध्यमाः ।\nनियोजयेद्यथावत्तांस्त्रिविधेष्वेव कर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men are of three kinds, king: the best, the worst and the middling. One should assign them to the three kinds of tasks accordingly."}},{"n":57,"text":"त्रय एवाधना राजन्भार्या दासस्तथा सुतः ।\nयत्ते समधिगच्छन्ति यस्य ते तस्य तद्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Only three have no property, king: wife, servant and son. Whatever they earn belongs to the one whose they are."}},{"n":58,"text":"चत्वारि राज्ञा तु महाबलेन\nवर्ज्यान्याहुः पण्डितस्तानि विद्यात् ।\nअल्पप्रज्ञैः सह मन्त्रं न कुर्या-\nन्न दीर्घसूत्रैरलसैश्चारणैश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise know four things that a very mighty king should avoid: do not take counsel with the slow-witted, with the procrastinating, the lazy, or flatterers."}},{"n":59,"text":"चत्वारि ते तात गृहे वसन्तु\nश्रियाभिजुष्टस्य गृहस्थधर्मे ।\nवृद्धो ज्ञातिरवसन्नः कुलीनः\nसखा दरिद्रो भगिनी चानपत्या ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let four stay in your house, dear friend, as one blessed with prosperity in the householder's duty: an aged kinsman, a fallen man of good family, a poor friend, and a childless sister."}},{"n":60,"text":"चत्वार्याह महाराज सद्यस्कानि बृहस्पतिः ।\nपृच्छते त्रिदशेन्द्राय तानीमानि निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brihaspati, great king, told Indra of the gods four things that give instant results; hear them from me."}},{"n":61,"text":"देवतानां च संकल्पमनुभावं च धीमताम् ।\nविनयं कृतविद्यानां विनाशं पापकर्मणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The intention of the gods, the power of the wise, the humility of the learned, and the destruction of evildoers."}},{"n":62,"text":"पञ्चाग्नयो मनुष्येण परिचर्याः प्रयत्नतः ।\nपिता माताग्निरात्मा च गुरुश्च भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man should carefully tend five fires, bull of the Bharatas: father, mother, the fire, the self, and the teacher."}},{"n":63,"text":"पञ्चैव पूजयँल्लोके यशः प्राप्नोति केवलम् ।\nदेवान्पितॄन्मनुष्यांश्च भिक्षूनतिथिपञ्चमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honoring five alone in the world brings pure fame: the gods, the ancestors, men, mendicants, and, as the fifth, guests."}},{"n":64,"text":"पञ्च त्वानुगमिष्यन्ति यत्र यत्र गमिष्यसि ।\nमित्राण्यमित्रा मध्यस्था उपजीव्योपजीविनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Five will follow you wherever you go: friends, enemies, neutrals, those who depend on you and those on whom you depend."}},{"n":65,"text":"पञ्चेन्द्रियस्य मर्त्यस्य छिद्रं चेदेकमिन्द्रियम् ।\nततोऽस्य स्रवति प्रज्ञा दृतेः पादादिवोदकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If one of the five senses of a mortal has a leak, his wisdom drains out of it like water from the foot of a leather bag."}},{"n":66,"text":"षड्दोषाः पुरुषेणेह हातव्या भूतिमिच्छता ।\nनिद्रा तन्द्री भयं क्रोध आलस्यं दीर्घसूत्रता ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who wants prosperity must give up six faults: sleep, drowsiness, fear, anger, laziness and procrastination."}},{"n":67,"text":"षडिमान्पुरुषो जह्याद्भिन्नां नावमिवार्णवे ।\nअप्रवक्तारमाचार्यमनधीयानमृत्विजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man should abandon these six like a broken boat on the sea: a teacher who does not teach, a priest who does not study,"}},{"n":68,"text":"अरक्षितारं राजानं भार्यां चाप्रियवादिनीम् ।\nग्रामकामं च गोपालं वनकामं च नापितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"a king who does not protect, a wife who speaks unkindly, a cowherd who wants a village, and a barber who wants a forest."}},{"n":69,"text":"षडेव तु गुणाः पुंसा न हातव्याः कदाचन ।\nसत्यं दानमनालस्यमनसूया क्षमा धृतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But six virtues should never be abandoned by a man: truth, giving, lack of laziness, freedom from envy, patience and steadiness."}},{"n":70,"text":"षण्णामात्मनि नित्यानामैश्वर्यं योऽधिगच्छति ।\nन स पापैः कुतोऽनर्थैर्युज्यते विजितेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who gains mastery over the six that are always within himself, being master of his senses, how could he be touched by sins and evils?"}},{"n":71,"text":"षडिमे षट्सु जीवन्ति सप्तमो नोपलभ्यते ।\nचोराः प्रमत्ते जीवन्ति व्याधितेषु चिकित्सकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These six live off six, and no seventh is found: thieves live off the careless, physicians off the sick,"}},{"n":72,"text":"प्रमदाः कामयानेषु यजमानेषु याजकाः ।\nराजा विवदमानेषु नित्यं मूर्खेषु पण्डिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"women off the lustful, priests off those who sacrifice, kings off the quarreling, and the wise off fools, always."}},{"n":73,"text":"सप्त दोषाः सदा राज्ञा हातव्या व्यसनोदयाः ।\nप्रायशो यैर्विनश्यन्ति कृतमूलाश्च पार्थिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king should always give up the seven faults that bring ruin, by which kings, even those firmly rooted, mostly perish."}},{"n":74,"text":"स्त्रियोऽक्षा मृगया पानं वाक्पारुष्यं च पञ्चमम् ।\nमहच्च दण्डपारुष्यमर्थदूषणमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Women, dice, hunting, drink, harsh speech as the fifth, great harshness in punishment, and misuse of wealth."}},{"n":75,"text":"अष्टौ पूर्वनिमित्तानि नरस्य विनशिष्यतः ।\nब्राह्मणान्प्रथमं द्वेष्टि ब्राह्मणैश्च विरुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eight are the signs beforehand of a man about to perish: first he hates brahmins and quarrels with brahmins."}},{"n":76,"text":"ब्राह्मणस्वानि चादत्ते ब्राह्मणांश्च जिघांसति ।\nरमते निन्दया चैषां प्रशंसां नाभिनन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He takes brahmins' property and wishes to kill brahmins; he delights in insulting them and does not welcome their praise."}},{"n":77,"text":"नैतान्स्मरति कृत्येषु याचितश्चाभ्यसूयति ।\nएतान्दोषान्नरः प्राज्ञो बुद्ध्या बुद्ध्वा विवर्जयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He does not remember them in his tasks and resents them when asked. A wise man should recognize these faults with his mind and avoid them."}},{"n":78,"text":"अष्टाविमानि हर्षस्य नवनीतानि भारत ।\nवर्तमानानि दृश्यन्ते तान्येव सुसुखान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"These eight, Bharata, are like fresh butter of joy, seen in the present, and they bring great happiness."}},{"n":79,"text":"समागमश्च सखिभिर्महांश्चैव धनागमः ।\nपुत्रेण च परिष्वङ्गः संनिपातश्च मैथुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting with friends, a great gain of wealth, embracing a son, and union in love."}},{"n":80,"text":"समये च प्रियालापः स्वयूथेषु च संनतिः ।\nअभिप्रेतस्य लाभश्च पूजा च जनसंसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pleasant talk at the right time, humility among one's own people, getting what one wants, and honor in the assembly of people."}},{"n":81,"text":"नवद्वारमिदं वेश्म त्रिस्थूणं पञ्चसाक्षिकम् ।\nक्षेत्रज्ञाधिष्ठितं विद्वान्यो वेद स परः कविः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who knows this house with nine doors, three pillars and five witnesses, presided over by the knower of the field, is a wise seer beyond others."}},{"n":82,"text":"दश धर्मं न जानन्ति धृतराष्ट्र निबोध तान् ।\nमत्तः प्रमत्त उन्मत्तः श्रान्तः क्रुद्धो बुभुक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ten do not know dharma, Dhritarashtra; learn them: the intoxicated, the careless, the mad, the weary, the angry, the hungry,"}},{"n":83,"text":"त्वरमाणश्च भीरुश्च लुब्धः कामी च ते दश ।\nतस्मादेतेषु भावेषु न प्रसज्जेत पण्डितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the hasty, the fearful, the greedy and the lustful. Therefore a wise man should not be attached to these states."}},{"n":84,"text":"अत्रैवोदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nपुत्रार्थमसुरेन्द्रेण गीतं चैव सुधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this they recount an ancient tale, sung for the sake of his son by the king of the asuras, Sudhanva."}},{"n":85,"text":"यः काममन्यू प्रजहाति राजा\nपात्रे प्रतिष्ठापयते धनं च ।\nविशेषविच्छ्रुतवान्क्षिप्रकारी\nतं सर्वलोकः कुरुते प्रमाणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king who gives up desire and anger, places wealth in a worthy person, is discerning, learned and prompt, the whole world takes as its standard."}},{"n":86,"text":"जानाति विश्वासयितुं मनुष्या-\nन्विज्ञातदोषेषु दधाति दण्डम् ।\nजानाति मात्रां च तथा क्षमां च\nतं तादृशं श्रीर्जुषते समग्रा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who knows how to win men's trust, inflicts punishment on those whose faults are known, who knows measure and forgiveness, all prosperity serves such a man."}},{"n":87,"text":"सुदुर्बलं नावजानाति कंचि-\nद्युक्तो रिपुं सेवते बुद्धिपूर्वम् ।\nन विग्रहं रोचयते बलस्थैः\nकाले च यो विक्रमते स धीरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He does not despise even the very weak, deals with an enemy wisely and alertly, does not like war with the strong, and shows courage at the right time: he is steadfast."}},{"n":88,"text":"प्राप्यापदं न व्यथते कदाचि-\nदुद्योगमन्विच्छति चाप्रमत्तः ।\nदुःखं च काले सहते जितात्मा\nधुरंधरस्तस्य जिताः सपत्नाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is never shaken on meeting misfortune, seeks effort and is alert, bears suffering in its time, self-controlled; his rivals are beaten by that bearer of the yoke."}},{"n":89,"text":"अनर्थकं विप्रवासं गृहेभ्यः\nपापैः संधिं परदाराभिमर्शम् ।\nदम्भं स्तैन्यं पैशुनं मद्यपानं\nन सेवते यः स सुखी सदैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who avoids pointless absence from home, alliance with sinners, touching another's wife, deceit, theft, slander and drinking, is always happy."}},{"n":90,"text":"न संरम्भेणारभतेऽर्थवर्ग-\nमाकारितः शंसति तथ्यमेव ।\nन मात्रार्थे रोचयते विवादं\nनापूजितः कुप्यति चाप्यमूढः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He does not begin his affairs in a rage, speaks only the truth when asked, does not like quarrels over trifles, and, unfoolish, is not angry when unhonored."}},{"n":91,"text":"न योऽभ्यसूयत्यनुकम्पते च\nन दुर्बलः प्रातिभाव्यं करोति ।\nनात्याह किंचित्क्षमते विवादं\nसर्वत्र तादृग्लभते प्रशंसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who is not envious but is compassionate, is not weak enough to stand surety, does not overspeak and bears disputes, wins praise everywhere."}},{"n":92,"text":"यो नोद्धतं कुरुते जातु वेषं\nन पौरुषेणापि विकत्थतेऽन्यान् ।\nन मूर्च्छितः कटुकान्याह किंचि-\nत्प्रियं सदा तं कुरुते जनोऽपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who never wears showy dress, does not boast of his manliness before others, and, not dazed, never speaks bitter words: people always hold him dear."}},{"n":93,"text":"न वैरमुद्दीपयति प्रशान्तं\nन दर्पमारोहति नास्तमेति ।\nन दुर्गतोऽस्मीति करोति मन्युं\nतमार्यशीलं परमाहुरग्र्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He does not stir up a quenched enmity, does not climb into pride or sink down, does not rage, thinking \"I am ruined\": him they call the best, of noble character."}},{"n":94,"text":"न स्वे सुखे वै कुरुते प्रहर्षं\nनान्यस्य दुःखे भवति प्रतीतः ।\nदत्त्वा न पश्चात्कुरुतेऽनुतापं\nन कत्थते सत्पुरुषार्यशीलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He does not exult in his own happiness, is not delighted at another's sorrow, does not regret afterward what he has given, and does not boast: he is a good man of noble character."}},{"n":95,"text":"देशाचारान्समयाञ्जातिधर्मा-\nन्बुभूषते यस्तु परावरज्ञः ।\nस तत्र तत्राधिगतः सदैव\nमहाजनस्याधिपत्यं करोति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who wishes to know local customs, agreements and the duties of castes, and knows high and low, wherever he goes always gains authority over the people."}},{"n":96,"text":"दम्भं मोहं मत्सरं पापकृत्यं\nराजद्विष्टं पैशुनं पूगवैरम् ।\nमत्तोन्मत्तैर्दुर्जनैश्चापि वादं\nयः प्रज्ञावान्वर्जयेत्स प्रधानः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise man who avoids hypocrisy, delusion, envy, sinful acts, enmity with the king, slander, quarrels with groups, and arguments with the drunk, the mad and the wicked, is foremost."}},{"n":97,"text":"दमं शौचं दैवतं मङ्गलानि\nप्रायश्चित्तं विविधाँल्लोकवादान् ।\nएतानि यः कुरुते नैत्यकानि\nतस्योत्थानं देवता राधयन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who daily practices self-control, purity, worship of the gods, auspicious rites, atonement and various worldly usages, his rise the gods favor."}},{"n":98,"text":"समैर्विवाहं कुरुते न हीनैः\nसमैः सख्यं व्यवहारं कथाश्च ।\nगुणैर्विशिष्टांश्च पुरोदधाति\nविपश्चितस्तस्य नयाः सुनीताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He marries among equals, not inferiors; with equals he has friendship, dealings and talk; he puts forward the more virtuous; the policies of such a wise man are well conducted."}},{"n":99,"text":"मितं भुङ्क्ते संविभज्याश्रितेभ्यो\nमितं स्वपित्यमितं कर्म कृत्वा ।\nददात्यमित्रेष्वपि याचितः सं-\nस्तमात्मवन्तं प्रजहत्यनर्थाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He eats moderately after sharing with his dependents, sleeps moderately after doing much work, and gives even to enemies when asked: misfortunes forsake that self-controlled man."}},{"n":100,"text":"चिकीर्षितं विप्रकृतं च यस्य\nनान्ये जनाः कर्म जानन्ति किंचित् ।\nमन्त्रे गुप्ते सम्यगनुष्ठिते च\nस्वल्पो नास्य व्यथते कश्चिदर्थः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When others do not know anything of what he intends or has done, and his counsel is kept secret and well carried out, not even a small matter of his goes wrong."}},{"n":101,"text":"यः सर्वभूतप्रशमे निविष्टः\nसत्यो मृदुर्दानकृच्छुद्धभावः ।\nअतीव संज्ञायते ज्ञातिमध्ये\nमहामणिर्जात्य इव प्रसन्नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who is devoted to the peace of all beings, truthful, gentle, generous and pure in heart, shines greatly among his kinsmen, like a clear great jewel of fine birth."}},{"n":102,"text":"य आत्मनापत्रपते भृशं नरः\nस सर्वलोकस्य गुरुर्भवत्युत ।\nअनन्ततेजाः सुमनाः समाहितः\nस्वतेजसा सूर्य इवावभासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who feels great shame in himself becomes a teacher to the whole world; with endless splendor, kindly and composed, he shines with his own radiance like the sun."}},{"n":103,"text":"वने जाताः शापदग्धस्य राज्ञः\nपाण्डोः पुत्राः पञ्च पञ्चेन्द्रकल्पाः ।\nत्वयैव बाला वर्धिताः शिक्षिताश्च\nतवादेशं पालयन्त्याम्बिकेय ॥","meaning":{"en":"The five sons of King Pandu, who was burned by a curse, born in the forest, like five Indras, were raised and taught by you when they were boys; they obey your command, son of Ambika."}},{"n":104,"text":"प्रदायैषामुचितं तात राज्यं\nसुखी पुत्रैः सहितो मोदमानः ।\nन देवानां नापि च मानुषाणां\nभविष्यसि त्वं तर्कणीयो नरेन्द्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given them their rightful kingdom, dear friend, you will be happy and glad with your sons; and you will not be a subject of suspicion to gods or men, king."}}]}]}